# Path Dependency CI

RULE: Clone path dependencies to `../repo-name` in CI. pyproject.toml must use `path = "../repo-name"`. Never use `deps/` for path deps. Use `${DEP_BRANCH:-main}` in CI clone steps to resolve feature branches.
WHY: Local workspace has repos as siblings; CI clone to `../` creates same layout. `deps/` breaks `uv pip install -e ".[dev]"`. Feature branch builds must install the dep's feature branch, not main.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/feature-branch-workflow.md, 06-coding-standards/dependency-management.md

## Standard CI Clone (GitHub Actions)

```yaml
# .github/workflows/quality-gates.yml — dep clone step
- name: Clone unified-config-interface
  run: |
    DEP_BRANCH="${{ github.event.pull_request.head.label || 'main' }}"
    # Extract dep branch from PR label "dep-branch: feat/X" if present
    PR_DEP_BRANCH=$(gh pr view ${{ github.event.pull_request.number }} \
      --json labels --jq '.labels[].name | select(startswith("dep-branch: ")) | ltrimstr("dep-branch: ")' \
      2>/dev/null || echo "")
    BRANCH="${PR_DEP_BRANCH:-main}"
    # Fall back to main if feature branch doesn't exist in dep repo
    if git ls-remote --heads https://github.com/org/unified-config-interface "$BRANCH" | grep -q "$BRANCH"; then
      git clone -b "$BRANCH" https://github.com/org/unified-config-interface ../unified-config-interface
    else
      git clone https://github.com/org/unified-config-interface ../unified-config-interface
    fi
    uv pip install --system -e ../unified-config-interface
```

## pyproject.toml path dep declaration

```toml
[tool.uv.sources]
unified-config-interface = { path = "../unified-config-interface", editable = true }
unified-cloud-interface = { path = "../unified-cloud-interface", editable = true }
```

## DO

```bash
git clone -b ${DEP_BRANCH:-main} ... ../unified-trading-library
# or with fallback:
git ls-remote --heads origin ${DEP_BRANCH} && \
  git clone -b ${DEP_BRANCH} ... ../unified-trading-library || \
  git clone ... ../unified-trading-library
uv pip install --system -e ../unified-trading-library
uv pip install --system -e ".[dev]"
```

## NEVER

```bash
git clone ... deps/unified-trading-library   # wrong path, breaks uv resolution
git clone ... unified-trading-library        # missing ../ prefix
# Clone without branch fallback — always use ${DEP_BRANCH:-main} or ls-remote check
```

## How DEP_BRANCH propagates

1. Dev runs: `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: X" --dep-branch "feat/X"` on repo-B
2. Quickmerge Stage 5 creates PR with label `dep-branch: feat/X`
3. GitHub Actions reads the label → sets `BRANCH=feat/X`
4. CI clones repo-A (a dep of repo-B) at branch `feat/X` if it exists, else `main`
5. uv installs from the cloned path → quality gates run against the feature version of repo-A
